show_report version=1 id=b0000011-0011-0011-0011-000000000011

@prompt
A list holds many values of the same type, written `[a, b, c]`, with type `[T]`.

# Task
Make `garden` the list of these four base waters: `250`, `180`, `50`, `200`.

@hint
A list of four integers.

@reference
### Lists
```hazel
[1, 2, 3]
```
A list of integers has type `[Int]`.

### List functions
- `length(xs)` how many elements
- `nth(xs, 0)` the element at an index

@hints
garden should be [250, 180, 50, 200].

@code
let garden: [Int] = [] in # fill me #
^^probe(nth(garden, 0))
+ ^^probe(nth(garden, 1))
+ ^^probe(nth(garden, 2))
+ ^^probe(nth(garden, 3))

@test
test garden == [250, 180, 50, 200] end
